nmap -sS domain(tcp syn stealth scan popular 1000 port)
nmap -sU domain(udp scan popular 1000 port)
nmap -sT domain(tcp connect scan popular 1000 port)
nmap -sN domain(tcp null scan sends null packet to the target)
nmap -p 21,22 domain(tcp syn stealth scan and specified the ports)
nmap -p- domain(tcp syn stealth Scan all ports 65535)
nmap -p 1-200 domain(tcp syn stealth the specified ports)
nmap --top-ports 100 domain(checks the most popular number of ports)
nmap -il list.txt(scan a list of ip or domains)
nmap -sn domain(try to ping to the host to know its up or not)
nmap -il -sn list.txt(scan a list of ip or domains and will ping it)
nmap -p 21 -A domain(gives more information about the ports and the service)
nmap -p 21 -A -v domain(gives more  information about the port and the service )
nmap -O domain(it gives the operation system that the ip working on) 
nmap -sC -Pn -sS -sV -p 22 domain(very important)
